      "content": "While diet can help with general wellness, attempting to correct a suspected mineral imbalance without testing is risky, especially with kidney disease. Instead of relying on coconut water, which can be high in potassium, try drinking plenty of plain water to ensure you are well-hydrated. For muscle cramps, gentle stretching and massaging the affected areas can sometimes provide immediate, safe relief.",
